title op6: a multi-name delta that stays inside one fragment

# Shape three of four for the PENDING set-delta proposal, and THE
# ONLY ONE OF THE FOUR WHOSE VERDICT THE PROPOSAL CHANGES.  See
# op6-split-quiet.tree for the gold policy.
#
# Onto un-shares z.  Off-of renames two names, x to aa and y to bb,
# so the delta is lost {x, y} gained {aa, bb}.  Both lost names lie
# in the SAME fragment -- the one onto left holding x and y.
#
# Today Definition 9.3 tries to pair each gained name with a lost one,
# succeeds only when there is exactly one of each, and degrades
# everything else: the gains become attachments, the attachment links
# meet the split's exclusions, and pass 2 reports a pooling conflict
# over a region where the two sides did not actually disagree about
# anything.  Off-of renamed two names; onto un-shared a third; no
# name is claimed twice.
#
# Under the proposal succession is set-valued, so there is nothing to
# pair.  The whole delta routes wholesale to the fragment holding its
# lost names, which is determined because the lost set does not
# straddle the split.  The fragment keeps its dnode and takes both
# new names.  Clean.
#
# Today:                conflict pooling, the region falls back to
#                       onto, and the gold below records that.
# Under the proposal:   clean, with
#
#                         tree expected
#                           1-1: /
#                             2-100: shared
#                               10-100: aa = v0
#                               10-100: bb
#                               30-200: z = v0
#
# CONFIDENCE.  The verdict and the fallback shape follow the pattern
# of the two-renames/ arm of 6-ambiguous-succession.tree, which is
# this same shape inside a larger fixture and which the engine has
# actually run.  The QUARANTINE SET is the least certain line here:
# it is derived by analogy with that fixture, which quarantines every
# name of the affected region under onto's names, including the
# split-off one.  If the engine quarantines a different set, check
# that fixture before assuming this one is wrong.
#
# Worth recording plainly: of the four op6 shapes, three decide the
# same way before and after the proposal, and the fourth conflicts
# both ways for different reasons.  This fixture is the ONLY place
# where the gold tier can see set-delta succession arrive at all.

tree base
  1-1: /
    2-100: shared/
      10-100: x = v0
      10-100: y
      10-100: z

tree onto
  1-1: /
    2-100: shared/
      10-100: x = v0
      10-100: y
      30-200: z = v0

tree offof
  1-1: /
    2-100: shared/
      10-100: aa = v0
      10-100: bb
      10-100: z

# --- expected result, worked by hand 2026-08-31 ---
expect conflict pooling
expect quarantined /shared/x
expect quarantined /shared/y
expect quarantined /shared/z

tree expected
  1-1: /
    2-100: shared
      10-100: x = v0
      10-100: y
      30-200: z = v0
